session 19: the harvest and the driver hardened before the run, and a preflight for the pod

Read before the first repository is listed. fetch_gh.py: the file budget is reached when no eligible directory can still fit (a budget one or two files short would have kept the harvest reading the whole pool); longer waits on a rate limit and on a throttled tarball; an unreadable tarball or an incomplete extraction is logged and skipped instead of stopping the harvest; history is fetched without credentials or prompts. s19_run.sh: stop when more than 10 percent of the tarballs fail; check the files on the disk before embedding and rebuild the corpus by commit id if a stop wiped it; run a registered follow-up after the outputs are pushed. s19_preflight.sh: tools, the self-test in the pod's Python and the real endpoints on a throwaway draw (seed 7, suffix _p19), no retrieval number. BRIEF.md lists the amendments; no definition, cell, test or reading changes. scripts/s19_selftest.py passes on the patched code.

